## English

Per-session color tags for DeepSeek Harness: hover a sidebar session row to pick a color, and tagged sessions stand out at a glance.

### Features

**🎨 Hover-to-color in the sidebar**

Rest the pointer on any session row in the sidebar and a color dot appears at the row's left edge. Click it for the palette — 12 preset colors plus one-click clear, applied instantly. No need to open the session.

- The dot reflects state: filled for tagged sessions, dashed outline otherwise
- The palette flips at screen edges so it never overflows
- A 160ms hover dwell keeps quick scanning free of pop-ups

**🌈 Colored session rows**

Tagged rows show a matching 3px bar on their left edge, so the session you want is findable at a glance across parallel work. Colors survive session switches, page reloads, and app restarts.

**💾 Host-side persistence**

Colors live in the Harness host's `storages/session-colors.json` with a localStorage mirror in the browser:

- Survives restarts and browser switches
- Instant first paint (mirror renders first, then reconciles with the host)
- Readable even while the host API is briefly unreachable; re-syncs on recovery

### Install

**Option 1 — plugin market (recommended)**

Settings → Plugin Market → search `session-colors` → install → refresh the page.

**Option 2 — CLI**

```sh
dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-session-colors
```

**Option 3 — local link (development)**

Symlink the package into the web profile's `node_modules`, then register it in the profile `package.json` (`dependencies` + `dsh.profile.bundles`).

### How it works

- **Host half**: a zero-dependency cordis plugin that registers a `/session-colors` route on the Harness webserver and persists the `sessionId → color` map as JSON (temp file + atomic rename; a corrupted store self-heals on the next write).
- **Client half**: a lazy-CJS `__ModuleLoader__` bundle with zero runtime dependencies. Harness ships no slot for session rows, so sidebar coloring matches session titles to row title spans exactly (unread-noise safe, DOM-order queue for duplicate titles, substring-trap guarded). A match failure only affects painting — never the data.

### HTTP API

| Method | Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/session-colors/api/colors` | Full map `{ colors: { [sessionId]: "#rrggbb" } }` |
| `PUT` | `/session-colors/api/colors/:sessionId` | Set a color, body `{"color": "#ef4444"}`; `null` clears |
| `DELETE` | `/session-colors/api/colors/:sessionId` | Clear one session's color |

Colors accept `#rgb` / `#rrggbb` hex (normalized to lowercase 6-digit); session ids are validated before storage.

### Compatibility & limitations

- Ships as a standard `dsh.bundle` plugin package; works in DeepSeek Harness Web and Desktop
- Sidebar painting is DOM-matched (best-effort): same-title rows consume colors in list order; blank/untitled sessions are never matched; a future Harness release that changes the row structure may disable painting — picking and data are unaffected
- Node ≥ 22.19 / ≥ 24

### Development

```sh
node smoke-host.js                    # host-half offline smoke tests (14 checks)
node smoke-host-phase2.js <temp-dir>  # corrupted-store recovery test
npm i --no-save jsdom                 # only the DOM test needs it
node smoke-client-dom.js              # client-half jsdom tests (15 checks)
```

